## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Design Decisions:**
> 1. **Fleet Table Layout**: Columns will be:
>    1. `Date of Dispatch`
>    2. `Truck Details` (shows Plate, Model, Capacity in Litres, and a badge if Subcontracted/Non-Company)
>    3. `Litres Loaded`
>    4. `From`
>    5. `Destination`
>    6. `Product`
>    7. `Transport`
>    8. `Mileage Cost`
>    9. `Extra Expenses`
>    10. `Balance` (For company trucks: `Transport - Mileage - Extra`; for subcontracted/non-company trucks: `Agreed Commission`)
>    11. `Actions` (📄 BOL, View Truck, Delete)
> 2. **Non-Company / Subcontracted Trucks**:
>    - When registering a truck, users can specify **Ownership**: `Company Owned` or `Subcontracted / Third-Party`.
>    - For Subcontracted trucks, an `agreed_commission` (or percentage) is set. On dispatch, the balance represents the company's agreed commission.
> 3. **Individual Truck Profile & Report**:
>    - Clicking any truck navigates to `/trucks/view/{id}`, displaying its dedicated dashboard, trip history, total volume hauled, maintenance history, and financial yield.
>    - A dedicated **Truck Performance Report** will be accessible under Reports (`/reports/trucks`) and directly from the Trucks section.

